# Tests and benchmarks

Product C++ under **`src/`**, **`core/`**, **`algorithm/`**, and **`testing/`** registers tests and benchmarks through **`//testing/test.gni`** and **`//testing/benchmark.gni`**.

## Tests (`gtest`)

- `test("name")` links **`//third_party:gtest`** (`gtest` + `gtest_main`). One behavior per **`TEST` / `TEST_F`**. Assertions are **`EXPECT_*` / `ASSERT_*`**.
- Do not add a handwritten `main` that walks cases, counts failures, and prints OK.
- **`use_gtest = false`** only when the binary is not a gtest runner. Say why in that `BUILD.gn`.
- When editing a file that still uses a local `expect` + `main`, migrate that file in the same change.

## Benchmarks (`google benchmark`)

- `benchmark("name")` links **`//third_party:gbenchmark`** and, by default, **`gbenchmark_main`**. Cases are **`BENCHMARK` / `BENCHMARK_F`**.
- Do not time with a handwritten loop and `printf`.
- **`use_benchmark_main = false`** only when the bench must skip (GPU / env). Then call `benchmark::Initialize` and `RunSpecifiedBenchmarks`.

## Out of scope

- `testing/tools` harness and `SmartGIS.exe --harness` stay product gates, not gtest.
- `third_party/` and `branches/` keep their own runners.

